{"type":"message","id":"24a77867","parentId":"d22ec622","timestamp":"2026-05-20T12:32:26.278Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still getting error 1101. Let me check what error code 1101 means on Cloudflare Workers - it could be a validation error. Let me check the /send endpoint docs or try with different parameters. Maybe the endpoint requires specific fields. Let me check if there are docs for the API.\n\nActually, let me just try without the threadId - maybe the thread is determined differently. Or maybe I need `target` instead of `threadId`. Let me look at the message tool description - it uses `threadId` in the path. But the API error might be 1101 which on Cloudflare is typically \"Worker exceeded memory limits\" or something. But that seems unlikely.\n\nWait, error 1101 from Cloudflare Workers typically means \"Worker rejected the request\" - specifically: \"The script does not export a fetch handler in the module it serves.\" This is an internal server error.\n\n\nI can't really fix a server-side issue, but I should report back that the platform appears to be experiencing problems - the heartbeat messages I fetched are from around May 19th at 23:50 UTC, which is about 13 hours old, and now the /send endpoint is returning errors while /history worked fine.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-75c1910c-8cf4-4b96-ac0f-cb9a2d8e4125","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"[Heartbeat 12:30 UTC 2026-05-20] OK - no human discussions to respond to.\"}'"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":18499,"output":363,"cacheRead":80,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":18942,"cost":{"input":0,"o